## At a glance

| Dimension | AgentOps | Tracify |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Primary focus** | Agent session recording | Integrated tracing + evaluation |
| **Recording fidelity** | High (detailed session capture) | Standard (traces) |
| **Evaluation** | Limited | Integrated |
| **Cost tracking** | Basic | Comprehensive |
| **Playback** | Native (session replay) | Trace replay only |
| **Best for** | Debugging agent execution | Production quality gates |

AgentOps records what agents did; Tracify evaluates what they should have done.

## Core difference

**AgentOps** focuses on *execution recording*: capture and replay agent sessions. **Tracify** focuses on *outcome evaluation*: assess whether agents achieved their goals.

## Scenario 1: debugging failed agent run

You need to understand exactly what the agent did step-by-step.

**With AgentOps:** Detailed session replay, action-by-action breakdown. Excellent for debugging.

**With Tracify:** Traces show execution but replay is less sophisticated.

**Result:** AgentOps wins on session replay.

## Scenario 2: production quality gates

You need hourly evaluations and regression detection.

**With AgentOps:** Recording works, but evaluation requires external tools.

**With Tracify:** Evaluation is integrated. Regression detection is automatic.

**Result:** Tracify wins on production automation.

## Cost and setup

**AgentOps:** Per-session pricing, works with frameworks
**Tracify:** All-in-one platform pricing

At scale with evaluation, Tracify is typically cheaper.

## When to choose each

**Choose AgentOps:** If session replay and debugging are critical
**Choose Tracify:** If production evaluation and cost tracking matter

## FAQ

{% faq-item question="Does AgentOps provide evaluation?" answer="Limited, requires external tools." /%}

{% faq-item question="Can I use both?" answer="Yes. AgentOps for replay, Tracify for evaluation." /%}

{% faq-item question="Which is cheaper?" answer="AgentOps for light debugging; Tracify for production at scale." /%}

